        "date": "2026-10-30T15:22:11Z"
      },
      "message": "DeepSeek: the EXL3 lend and the DMA read-back of host-summed pieces opt-in (MAYA_DS4_EXL3_LEND=1, DS4_AR_BACK_DMA=1), the lend never on one GPU (#691)\n\nNeither has run on our machines: there is no DeepSeek EXL3 pack on them, and the DMA read-back needs a\ntensor-parallel group of 5+ members and a CUDA 12.5+ build. Both stay as the pull request wrote them, off\nuntil measured here. The lend also refuses to load a layer split whose layers keep too few recent slots for\nthe chunk, where the same setup loaded before, and the pull request's own note says lent buffers gave wrong\nanswers on one GPU: the lend now needs two GPUs or more even when asked for.",
