  {
    "sha": "c7d08c58a5445e304b1f35a7da70b78c332615f5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOU-xXotoAKGM3ZDA4YzU4YTU0NDVlMzA0YjFmMzVhN2RhNzBiNzhjMzMyNjE1ZjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "needmorevram",
        "email": "needmorevram@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-30T11:39:41Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mw00",
        "email": "mw00@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-30T15:22:11Z"
      },
      "message": "DeepSeek: long prompts - restore points near the end kept in one read, a chunk streams only the experts it picks, EXL3 chunk buffers lent from the expert cache, host-summed pieces read back by DMA (#691)\n\nSquash of the pull request's 9 commits:\n\n- DeepSeek: a prompt's restore points near its end kept in one read (MAYA_DS4_MARKS_INSIDE; a read from token 0\n  still stops at a shared start, #607; a tail point taken on the way costs no stop, so #668's tail cost counts only\n  the reads that stop at it); maya-ds4 --marks-check compares the two reads\n- DeepSeek on CUDA: a short chunk (up to DS4_SKIP_UNPICKED_ROWS, 1536) streams only the experts it picks - the same\n  slots, batches and summing order\n- DeepSeek on CUDA: a device with a shallow ring skips unpicked experts on every chunk\n- maya-ds4: --ids @FILE reads the ids from a file (a long prompt's are more than one argument may hold)\n- DeepSeek: a group whose chunk sums the host makes pins no F32 rows for the copy engines' sums\n- DeepSeek: a chunk that skips unpicked experts reads their picks at pv_n (copy_ahead read them at n_slots + j once\n  VRAM slots were lent)\n- DeepSeek EXL3: a prompt's chunk buffers lent from the expert cache's recent slots (MAYA_DS4_EXL3_LEND;\n  DS4_CHECK_LEND=1 compares each lent slot before and after)\n- DeepSeek: a chunk's host-summed pieces read back by DMA behind a stream wait (DS4_AR_BACK_DMA; CUDA 12.5+, the\n  kernels as before where the driver refuses the wait)\n- DeepSeek EXL3: a lending GPU's layer that every expert fitted keeps one in RAM, so it has slots to lend\n\ndocs/SETTINGS.md: long prompts on two tensor-parallel groups (--tp 4 + DS4_SPLIT, a setting, not a default).\nDS4_RUN_TRACE=1: each device's timeline of a run of chunks.",
